// TEST: An unannotated parameter beside a float literal refuses an Int64 argument (rejects)
// ERROR: BL3019 @ 9:16
// ERROR-CONTAINS: Int64 + Float64 is Float64
// ============================================================================
// `x` is an anonymous `T` (functions/269), so `x + 1.0` is typed `T`, and the
// Int64 instance `addone(3)` would truncate the Float64 sum -- the same
// refusal as the spelled `x: T` (functions/229). `3` is an Int64 literal;
// write `addone(3.0)`.
function addone(x) = x + 1.0
let n = addone(3)
